Runtime arena: PS2X_RUNTIME_ARENA=<base>:<limit> keeps the runtime's guest allocations out of the game's heap.
Why: guestMalloc (SIF command packets, RPC buffers) allocated from the heap the game declares with SetupHeap, which
Jackass's Metrowerks malloc owns. Once FMOD's IOP-to-EE replies flowed (patch 05) its blocks were overwritten and
the heap walk (0x102420) looped forever on the main menu. With the arena set, the runtime allocates only there,
SetupHeap returns the game the heap base it asked for, and EndOfHeap reports the game's heap limit.
Unset: unchanged. Same idea as the Killzone recomp's runtime arena (its patch 0008).
Origin: this project (jackass-ps2-recomp), 2026-10-27.

